{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-26","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：整数","englishTitle":"If from an odd number an odd number be subtracted, the remainder will be even.","book":9,"number":26,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.26","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.26/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":26,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-26@raw-982ac61209ab9738","contentId":"euclid-9-26","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"982ac61209ab9738fad2664f8962650d71020a41a682d7e053b88606692e2dd3","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-26.statement","euclid-9-26.proof.1","euclid-9-26.proof.2","euclid-9-26.conclusion","euclid-9-26.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-26.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-26","revisionId":"euclid-9-26@raw-982ac61209ab9738","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"cfa29c613e1610dea27a86f8dd4981f7c40782158bc7a1f9fc7ccfd88317211f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If from an odd number an odd number be subtracted, the remainder will be even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果从一个奇数中减去一个奇数,则其余的为偶数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-26.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-26","revisionId":"euclid-9-26@raw-982ac61209ab9738","order":1,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b07d73d6baebce8395062f79fe6ecaac87105159f543d6a005f7be9dab52aa36","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For from the odd number AB let the odd number BC be subtracted; I say that the remainder CA is even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"奇数AB, 奇数BC 减掉; 我说其余的CA 都平了 。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-26.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-9-26","revisionId":"euclid-9-26@raw-982ac61209ab9738","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a63c86b3b3b0f6a4e11b0aa504c2a6e2f11becdb5c78b6a563682638dff146e0","citations":["euclid-7-def-7"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since AB is odd, let the unit BD be subtracted; therefore the remainder AD is even. [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,由于AB是奇数,所以,单位 BD是平数,因此其余的AD是平数。 [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-26.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-26","revisionId":"euclid-9-26@raw-982ac61209ab9738","order":3,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"403dddad6df1ef8fa4021aa000f6a3bb5877f2c732a2d37bd2bef77b557497e4","citations":["euclid-7-def-7","euclid-9-24"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For the same reason CD is also even; [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)] so that the remainder CA is also even. [[IX. 24](/principles/euclid-9-24)] Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"出于同样原因,CD也是偶数;因此,其余的CA也是偶数。 [[VII. Def. 7](/principles/euclid-7-def-7)] [[IX. 24](/principles/euclid-9-24)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-26.source","contentId":"euclid-9-26","revisionId":"euclid-9-26@raw-982ac61209ab9738","order":4,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d7a586a79774c